":"2025-09-12","eventType":"legislative_action","historyId":"118212769","location":"Assembly","sequence":23,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"In Assembly. Concurrence in Senate amendments pending.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-other","code":null,"date":"2025-09-13","eventType":"legislative_action","historyId":"118212770","location":"Assembly","sequence":24,"significance":"routine","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Joint Rules 61(a)(14) and 51(a)(4) suspended. (Ayes 59. Noes 20. Page 3413.)","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-concurred","code":null,"date":"2025-09-13","eventType":"concurred","historyId":"118212771","location":"Assembly","sequence":24,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Senate amendments concurred in. To Engrossing and Enrolling. (Ayes 59. Noes 19. Page 3452.).","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-enrolled","code":null,"date":"2025-09-24","eventType":"enrolled","historyId":"118212772","location":"Governor","sequence":25,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Enrolled and presented to the Governor at 3 p.m.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-approved","code":null,"date":"2025-10-13","eventType":"approved_by_governor","historyId":"118212773","location":"Governor","sequence":26,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Approved by the Governor.","time":null,"votes":[]},{"classificationRule":"ca-chaptered","code":null,"date":"2025-10-13","eventType":"chaptered","historyId":"118212774","location":"Secretary of State","sequence":27,"significance":"major","source":null,"status":null,"text":"Chaptered by Secretary of State - Chapter 730, Statutes of 2025.","time":null,"votes":[]}],"affectedStatutes":[{"action":"IS_ADDED","code":"ELEC","text":"Chapter 6.6 (commencing with Section 21554) is added to Division 21 of the Elections Code, to read:"}],"approvedDate":"2025-10-13","chapter":{"citation":"Chapter 730, Statutes of 2025","number":"730","type":"CHP","year":"2025"},"chapteredDate":"2025-10-13","committees":[],"conditions":[],"contentHash":"c494b9560da633655b7c126fc06622746fb399e8a46169b55ad4f5762d3502e5","cosponsorCount":null,"digest":"Existing law requires the board of supervisors, following a county’s decision to elect its board using district-based elections or following each decennial federal census for a county whose board is already elected using district-based elections, by ordinance or resolution, to adjust the boundaries of all of the supervisorial districts of the county so that the districts are as nearly equal in population as possible and comply with applicable federal law, and specifies the procedures the board of supervisors must follow in adjusting those boundaries. Existing law establishes independent redistricting commissions in the Counties of Los Angeles, San Diego, Orange, Riverside, San Luis Obispo, Kern, Fresno, and Sacramento, which are charged with adjusting the supervisorial district boundaries for their respective counties.\n\nThis bill would similarly establish the Citizens Redistricting Commission in the County of Merced, which would be charged with adjusting the boundary lines of the districts of the Board of Supervisors of the County of Merced in accordance with specified criteria. The commission would consist of 11 members who meet specified qualifications. By increasing the duties of local officials, the bill would impose a state-mandated local program.\n\nThis bill would make legislative findings and declarations as to the necessity of a special statute for the County of Merced.\n\nThe California Constitution requires the state to reimburse local agencies and school districts for certain costs mandated by the state. Statutory provisions establish procedures for making that reimbursement.\n\nThis bill would provide that, if the Commission on State Mandates determines that the bill contains costs mandated by the state, reimbursement for those costs shall be made pursuant to the statutory provisions noted above.","digestDate":null,"digestVersion":null,"effective":{"basis":"not_verified","date":null,"note":"No effective date is recorded in the official bill data and DemocracyHQ has not verified one. A non-urgency statute enacted in a regular session generally takes effect on January 1 after a 90-day period (Cal. Const. art. IV, § 8(c)), but a bill may state other operative dates."},"expiryClauses":[],"firstObservedAt":"2026-11-20T01:12:59Z","id":"ca-20252026-ab1441","identifier":"AB 1441","indicators":{"Appropriation":"NO","BudgetBill":"NO","Election":"NO","FiscalCommittee":"YES","ImmediateEffect":"NO","LocalProgram":"YES","TaxLevy":"NO","Urgency":"NO","UsualCurrentExpenses":"NO","VoteRequired":"MAJORITY"},"introducedDate":"2025-02-21","issueTags":[{"matchCount":null,"matchedField":"official subject line","matchedText":"County of Merced Citizens Redistricting Commission.","ruleId":"tag-redist-2","tag":"redistricting"}],"judicialNote":"Legislative status does not show whether a court has blocked, narrowed or upheld any provision. Check the linked litigation, which may be incomplete.","lastActionDate":"2025-10-13","lastActionText":"Chaptered by Secretary of State - Chapter 730, Statutes of 2025.","lastCheckedAt":"2026-11-27T19:32:34Z","leadAuthors":"Introduced by Assembly Member Soria","legislativeStatus":{"currentHouse":"Secretary of State","currentLocation":null,"currentStatus":"Chaptered","measureState":"Chaptered"},"legislativeSubjects":[],"measureType":"Assembly Bill","officialUrl":"https://leginfo.legislature.ca.gov/faces/billNavClient.xhtml?bill_id=202520260AB1441","policyArea":null,"relatedMeasures":[],"selection":{"matchedField":"official subject line (latest version)","matchedText":"Redistricting","ruleId":"ca-select-2"},"session":"2025-2026 Regular Session","shortTitles":[],"sourceId":"ca-leginfo-bulk","sourcePublishedAt":"2026-11-23T05:26:07Z","sourceRecordUrl":null,"sponsors":[],"state":